## First-time setup

1. **Create the Xcode project shell**
   Open Xcode → **File → New → Project → iOS → App**.
   - Product name: **MyoDoc** (not "수리수리" — Xcode wants an ASCII identifier; the Korean display name is set via `CFBundleDisplayName`)
   - Interface: SwiftUI · Language: Swift · Minimum iOS: 17.0
   - Organization identifier: e.g. `org.myopiamanage`
2. **Point the project at this folder's sources.** Delete the auto-generated `ContentView.swift` and the `MyoDocApp.swift` Xcode creates, then drag the files under `MyoDoc/` into the project (Create groups, add to the `MyoDoc` target). Make sure `Assets.xcassets` is in the target's "Copy Bundle Resources" phase.
3. **Install Swift packages** (File → Add Package Dependencies):
   - `https://github.com/google/GoogleSignIn-iOS`
   - `https://github.com/kakao/kakao-ios-sdk` (via Swift Package)
   - `https://github.com/naver/naveridlogin-sdk-ios-swift`
4. **Configure URL schemes & Info.plist keys** – copy the template at [`MyoDoc/Resources/Info.plist`](MyoDoc/Resources/Info.plist) into the target, or let Xcode auto-generate and copy individual keys. Details in [`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md § Auth configuration`](docs/ARCHITECTURE.md).
5. **Set backend base URL** in `MyoDoc/Core/Networking/APIConfig.swift` (or via the `API_BASE_URL` build setting referenced from `Info.plist`).
6. **Apply community-board database migration** on the backend:
   ```bash
   cd ~/code/myopia/myopiaBackend
   npx prisma migrate deploy
   ```
   The migration file is `prisma/migrations/20260515080000_community_board/migration.sql`.

